<!--
    kuna `rangefold`: a conditional branch on `V cmp K` bounds `V` in every
    block one of its out-edges controls.  A comparison of `V` against a
    constant whose outcome those ranges fix folds to `true` or `false`, so the
    branch on it goes away, and `V & 0xff` on a `V` the ranges keep below 256
    folds to `V`.

    Stage / sub-stage: P3 "simplification-quiescence".  The P0 assertion
    `option rangefold on|off` decides the fold; on is the default.

    The bytes are decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/rangefold.c
    built by gcc 15.3 at -O0 -fno-pie -no-pie -nostartfiles (x86-64 SysV):
    nested (`if (x < 10) { if (x > 20) ... }`), masked (`x & 0xff` under
    `x < 16`) and digit (a test of `c > '9'` inside `c >= '0' && c <= '9'`).

    Pass 1 runs with no option line, the shipped default (on).  Pass 2
    (`option rangefold off`) prints the decided tests.
-->
